{
  "title": "Compressor",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "A compressor for live",
        "sources: vocals and",
        "acoustic guitar on",
        "the line input, or",
        "anything in a chain.",
        "",
        "It adds no delay, so",
        "a singer monitoring",
        "through it hears",
        "themselves on time.",
        "",
        "Typical chain:",
        " Line In > Compressor",
        "",
        "Start from a preset,",
        "then set Threshold",
        "while watching GR."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Main Page",
      "lines": [
        "K1 Thrsh: level where",
        " compression starts",
        " (-60 to 0 dB)",
        "K2 Ratio: how hard",
        " it pushes back. 3",
        " means 3 dB over",
        " comes out as 1 dB",
        "K3 Atk: how fast it",
        " clamps down (ms)",
        "K4 Rel: how fast it",
        " lets go (ms)",
        "K5 Knee: width of the",
        " soft bend around",
        " the threshold",
        "K6 Gain: makeup gain",
        " after compressing",
        "K7 Mix: dry/wet, for",
        " parallel squashing",
        "K8 GR: the meter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Reading the Meter",
      "lines": [
        "GR shows how far the",
        "level is being turned",
        "down right now, in dB.",
        "The bar fills from",
        "the right; ticks mark",
        "3, 6 and 12 dB.",
        "",
        "Touch knob 8 to read",
        "it, plus the level",
        "the detector sees.",
        "",
        "Rough guide:",
        " 2-4 dB gentle",
        " 4-8 dB obvious",
        " 10+ dB squashed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Curve Page",
      "lines": [
        "Jog right from Main.",
        "",
        "Left: input level",
        "across, output up.",
        "The dotted diagonal",
        "is no compression;",
        "the solid line is",
        "what you have set.",
        "The dot is where the",
        "signal is now.",
        "",
        "The same 8 knobs",
        "work here, so turning",
        "Thrsh, Ratio or Knee",
        "bends the curve."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Setup Page",
      "lines": [
        "In: input gain before",
        " the compressor. Use",
        " it to hit the",
        " threshold harder.",
        " Presets leave it",
        " alone.",
        "HPF: high-pass on the",
        " detector only, so",
        " lows and pops do not",
        " pump the vocal. The",
        " audio keeps its",
        " bass.",
        "Det: Peak reacts to",
        " every transient; RMS",
        " follows loudness",
        " and is smoother.",
        "Auto: sets makeup",
        " gain to half the",
        " reduction a full",
        " scale signal gets.",
        " While on, the Gain",
        " knob is ignored.",
        "Byp: bypass, to A/B.",
        " On, you hear the",
        " input untouched;",
        " GR shows BYP and a",
        " ghost of what it",
        " would be doing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Presets",
      "lines": [
        "Default",
        "Vocal Leveler",
        " even, natural",
        "Vocal Upfront",
        " pop vocal, forward",
        "Vocal Gentle",
        " light touch",
        "Spoken Word",
        "Acoustic Strum",
        " keeps the pick",
        "Fingerpicked",
        "Parallel Crush",
        " heavy, mixed low",
        "Peak Catcher",
        " near-limiter",
        "Bus Glue",
        "Drum Punch",
        "",
        "Save your own with",
        "My Presets."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Tips",
      "lines": [
        "Vocals: lower Thrsh",
        "until GR swings",
        "3-6 dB on louder",
        "phrases, then bring",
        "back level with Gain.",
        "",
        "Pumping or breathing?",
        "Raise HPF, lengthen",
        "Rel, or use RMS.",
        "",
        "Lost the pick attack?",
        "Lengthen Atk.",
        "",
        "Is it better? Match",
        "the loudness first:",
        "set Gain so Byp On",
        "and Off sound equally",
        "loud, then compare.",
        "",
        "Too squashed but you",
        "like the density?",
        "Lower Mix."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
